{"event": "tool", "name": "finish", "args": {"summary": "## Answer: Average Unit Price by Category\n\n| Category | Average Unit Price ($) |\n|---|---|\n| Accessories | 32.50 |\n| Electronics | 275.71 |\n| Furniture | 191.05 |\n| Office Supplies | 11.37 |\n\n## Data Quality Issues Found & Fixed\n\n1. **Duplicate row (row 5)**: An exact duplicate of row 4 (Order_ID 2005). Removed the duplicate.\n\n2. **Misspelled Category labels**: \n   - Row 9: \"Office Suplies\" \u2192 corrected to \"Office Supplies\"\n   - Row 20: \"Furnture\" \u2192 corrected to \"Furniture\"\n\n3. **Negative Quantity values (rows 1, 34, 51)**: These rows had negative quantities (-8, -6, -2), violating the rule that Quantity must be a positive whole number (min: 1). These also produced negative Revenue values, inconsistent with the Revenue = Quantity \u00d7 Price formula. These 3 rows were excluded from the analysis.\n\n## Caveats\n- The Region column still has some whitespace variants (\" West\", \" South\", \"West \") and 2 missing values, but these do not affect the question about average unit price by category.\n- The analysis is based on 66 rows after cleaning (originally 70 rows)."}, "ok": true, "output": {"finished": true}, "t": 101.84}
